course: dictionary
lesson: 15800
title: Looks, offers and the prefix un-
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Unattractive has two parts: un- and attractive. The prefix un- means not, so unattractive means not attractive. «The old shed looked unattractive, with broken windows and peeling paint.» The clues are broken windows and peeling paint, so unattractive means not nice to look at.
explain: The word can also describe something that people do not want, not just something that looks bad. «The shop's offer was unattractive: it cost more than the toy was worth.» Nobody wants to buy at that price, so unattractive means not pleasant or not wanted. Ask: would someone choose this? If not, it is probably unattractive.
explain: Try the swap check. Put your meaning in place of the word: «The old shed looked not nice to look at, with broken windows and peeling paint.» It still makes sense, so your meaning is right.
fact: Unattractive is an adjective. It describes a noun, like a shed, a place, or an offer.
fact: The prefix un- means not, so attractive means pleasing to look at or wanted, and unattractive means the opposite.
fact: «Unattractive» can mean not nice to look at, or not pleasant so people do not want it.
fact: «An unattractive offer» is one that people will not choose, such as a price that is too high.
fact: Attractive is the opposite of unattractive. Words with un- often have an opposite without it.
exercise: «The old shed looked unattractive, with broken windows and peeling paint.» What does unattractive mean here? | Warm and cosy | Loud and noisy | *Not nice to look at | Very big and tall
exercise: Mia said the offer was unattractive, so nobody took it. What does unattractive mean here? | Very quick to finish | *Not pleasant, so people do not want it | Bright and shiny | Free and generous
exercise: Which part of unattractive means not? | ive | at | *un | tract
test: Which word is the opposite of unattractive? | dull | *attractive | ugly | plain
test: Which sentence uses unattractive correctly? | The party was unattractive because we all wanted to go. | The sunny beach looked unattractive, so we sat in the sand and smiled. | The unattractive puppy ran to hug everybody. | *A shop with rubbish piled outside looked unattractive to most shoppers.
exam: Which is an example of an unattractive offer? | A bag of sweets given to each friend | *A price so high that nobody would pay it | A game that every child asks to play again | A free ticket to the fair for everyone in the class
